SUMMARY:Santa Lights Manassas
DESCRIPTION:Santa Lights Manassas\, also known as the Tree Lighting\, has been a fixture in the Manassas community for over 32 years! It takes place on the Friday night before the Christmas Parade beginning at 5:30p.m. This year’s event takes place on Friday\, December 4. \nThe magic of the evening begins with holiday musical performances and then Santa arrives in Manassas shortly after 6p.m. After the tree is lit\, Santa and Mrs. Claus greet all the children and listen to their holiday wishes at the TD Santa & Mrs. Claus Meet & Greet at the Train Depot. Families can enjoy free wagon rides to get into the holiday spirit. The Harris Pavilion Ice Rink will be open for business as well as the Manassas Museum\, downtown shops and restaurants.
URL:https://historicmanassas.org/event/santa-lights-manassas-2/
LOCATION:Historic Downtown Manassas @ 9431 West St\, Manassas\, VA 20110\, USA\, Manassas\, VA\, United States
CATEGORIES:Arts,Winter Holiday
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/webp:https://historicmanassas.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/santalights.webp
GEO:38.792244;-77.511522
END:VEVENT
